target:    tests/oracle/classify.py
gate:      composer test:classifier-plants
kind:      boundary
expect:    P41-a-pin-on-one-arm-only-is-not-a-pin label
rationale: A window pinned on one side only leaves the other free to move, which is the state the pin exists to prevent - the comment on those two lines says exactly that, and until P41 nothing could tell whether the code did. The single clock plant carried pinned:false on both arms, so the flag space was one point.
---
diff --git a/tests/oracle/classify.py b/tests/oracle/classify.py
--- a/tests/oracle/classify.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/classify.py
@@ -597,7 +597,7 @@ def classify(triple, contract=None, register=None):
                   for name in ("clock_dependent", "calendar_day_dependent")),
         # BOTH arms must be pinned for the pin to help. A window pinned on one side only leaves
         # the other free to move, which is the state the pin exists to prevent.
-        pinned=_flag(old_env, "pinned") and _flag(new_env, "pinned"),
+        pinned=_flag(old_env, "pinned") or _flag(new_env, "pinned"),
         observable=observable,
         register_hit=hit,
         register_near=tuple(near),
